<title>UK: Banco General ups five-year bond to $115 million.</title>
<headline>Banco General ups five-year bond to $115 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco General SA has increased its five-year Eurobond to $115 million from $100 million, lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal, launched on Monday, has also been priced.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $115 MLN  COUPON     7.70	MATURITY    01.AUG.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.957    PAY DATE    06.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.25	REOFFER    99.957    SPREAD	+165 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BBB-	DENOMS (K) 10-250    SALE LIMITS US/GB/PA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  PANAMA    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    50 BP     SELL CONC  75 BP     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.0 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 31.JUL.02 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
